e and it's going to be a real  challenge for the Democratic Party which  is supposedly the party of the middle  class this the small guy of the small  gal to reconcile high-cost unreliable  energy with the common good but my book  talks about in Ron's early investments  in solar power wind power all with  government favor and the obama energy  plan would be the in ron energy plan  writ large for the hope for the whole  country  of Enron's strategy of sustainable  energy centered around wind power solar  power and major changes in energy  efficiency the obama energy plans is  centered around the exact same thing  that our energy future has to move away  from fossil fuels toward renewables and  so if you look back and see what Enron  was doing the rationale all that comes  into play with the obama energy plan and  that's something that's going to be  popularized against obama's energy  strategy  as far as my background I first became  interested in libertarian ideas in high  school when I read the fountainhead by  Ayn Rand I went to college became very  interested in free market economics  particularly Austrian school economics  and after college I received an advanced  degree in economics and was working for  a bank in Houston and they asked me to  do an industry study they got me very  deep into oil and gas regulation from  that I wrote a book from the for the  Cato Institute called oil gas and  government the US experience and then  after that was over I decided to go into  the business world and got an invitation  to join Enron and I got to know Ken Lay  the PhD chairman there he had a PhD in  economics and I worked there for 16  years and for the last seven years I was  director of public policy analysis on  the corporate level and one of my main  job was writing speeches for Ken Lay so  I got to know lay very well so when the  company collapsed I was in a very good  position to write my own history of  events and it was about at that time  that I became interested in Iran and  objectivism again when i saw the  collapse of enron i realized this was  right out of a 9r and novel and so when  I was writing my writing capitalism at  work i have a whole chapter devoted to  Rand's ideas which to me explain the  kennel a paradox about how a person who  superficially at least had all this  talent in all this energy and all this  vision ended up in practice being a  total failure and I think the insights  of Objectivism a philosophical fraud  come into play here something else  interesting about ein r and as I went  through her books and studied her  personal life I realized that she was  party to the Enron of the Objectivist  libertarian  movement and that is the breakup of the  Nathaniel Branden Institute back in 1968  and I have an appendix in the book  called the Iran problem where I draw  analogies between that event which  ruptured the libertarian objectivists  movement thousands of people were  bewildered and stranded because of that  analogizing that too Enron and I think  there's a number of parallels
 

